      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0011",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Instead, you must invoke the `NSObject` class method [`instancesRespond(to:)`](nsobject-swift.class/instancesrespond(to:).md) directly on the object’s superclass, as illustrated in the following code fragment.",
      "normalizedSource": "Instead, you must invoke the `NSObject` class method [`instancesRespond(to:)`](nsobject-swift.class/instancesrespond(to:).md) directly on the object’s superclass, as illustrated in the following code fragment.",
      "sourceHash": "828b1e0459c249c9440b50f4e805a5c5bce9eebf2692bdbd80421768c972120f",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Therefore, sending [`responds(to:)`](nsobjectprotocol/responds(to:).md) to `super` is equivalent to sending it to `self`.",
      "contextAfter": "```objc\nif( [MySuperclass instancesRespondToSelector:@selector(aMethod)] ) {\n    // invoke the inherited method\n    [super aMethod];\n}\n```",
